  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「マトア」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%9E%E3%83%88%E3%82%A2",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106376305,
      "text": "マトア (Matoa) またはタウン (Taun) は、ムクロジ科の常緑高木。和名はバンリュウガン（蕃竜眼）。高さは高いもので15mを超える。葉は偶数羽状複葉で小葉は4～9対の披針形鋭尖頭。白色の小さな花をつけ、2-5cmの果実には半透明の白い果肉が入り甘味が強く多汁で生食用。種子は焼食用。樹皮は薬用。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Pometia pinnata」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pometia_pinnata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1359901001,
      "text": "The Pometia pinnata is a tropical hardwood tree species that is widespread in the Pacific and Southeast Asian regions. The tree species has many common names, including matoa, tava, taun tree, Island lychee and Pacific lychee. The species comes from the Sapindaceae family and comes from the clades of Tracheophytes, Angiosperms, and the order Sapindales."
    }
  },
